The duo’s international footprint has expanded with remarkable speed. Following their initial entry onto Tokyo’s prestigious J-WAVE Top 100 in 2023, where they peaked at #25, KAGAMI achieved a major milestone with their *TIME MACHINE* EP, released on April 11, 2025, via Dontaku Records. The record has garnered millions of streams across Spotify and Apple Music, propelled by global radio play and key editorial playlist placements. Featuring collaborations with prominent Japanese artists like kiki vivi lily and Kan Sano, the project earned glowing coverage in leading South Korean and Japanese music magazines, establishing a dedicated listener base across the US, Europe, Taiwan, and South Korea. Building on this global momentum, the duo returned in June 2026 with "Perfect Wave," a perfectly timed summer single, accompanied by a cinematic music video featuring a special appearance by Korean content creator Charming Jo. The record has hit the airwaves on KEXP, KCRW, NTS and several other radio stations globally..

On stage, KAGAMI translates their intricate studio work into direct, dancefloor-ready live experiences. The duo performs a dynamic hybrid set where they layer vintage synthesizers, vocals & live vocoder, and DJing to reshape their tracks in real-time. Their performances have already graced major festival stages, including the North Sea Jazz Festival, MoMo Festival, Oerol and Wildeburg. Their captivating stage presence has also earned them support slots for boundary-pushing acts like Louis Cole, Dirty Loops and Yīn Yīn.

Following a successful summer tour across South Korea and a nationwide run as part of Popronde 2025, KAGAMI kicked off 2026 with a highly praised showcase at ESNS (Eurosonic Noorderslag) in Groningen, cementing their place as one of the most exciting electronic crossover acts in Europe. The duo is currently preparing their highly anticipated debut album, slated for release in 2027.

### **AT A GLANCE**

### **CURRENT RELEASES**

- **Single**: "Perfect Wave" (Dontaku Records, 2026)
- **EP**: *TIME MACHINE* (Dontaku Records, 2025)
- **EP**: *PHASE 1* (Dontaku Records, 2023)
- **Upcoming**: Debut Album (Slated for 2027)

### **SELECT PERFORMANCES & HIGHLIGHTS**

- **2026**: Wildeburg, Into the Woods, Oerol, ESNS (Eurosonic Noorderslag Showcase)
- **2025**: Popronde (Netherlands Nationwide Tour), South Korea Live Tour, Paradiso (Amsterdam, sold out)
- **Past Highlights**: North Sea Jazz Festival, MoMo Festival
- **Radio Plays:** KEXP, KCRW, NTS, J-Wave (Reached #25 on J-WAVE Top 100 (2023))
- **Highlights**: Over 4 million streams on *TIME MACHINE* EP, opening support for Louis Cole, Dirty Loops and Yīn Yīn.
